senses.gloss:
--a class of seers, ६०,000 in number, born of Kratu:
1: भा. III. १२. ४३; IV. 1. ३९; V. २१. १७; Br. I. 2. २७; Vi. I. १०. ११; II. १०. २२.
advised Citraratha, who fell to the ground to gather कौशिक's bones to throw them into the सरस्वती and get redemption;
2: भा. VI. 8. ४०.
They go in front of the Sun from his rise to his setting, singing his glory;
3: Ib. XII. ११. ४९; Br. II. ११. ३७; २१. ११५; २३. २८ and ४९, M. १२६. २८; वा. 2. २७; २३. १५९; २८. ३१; ५०. १६८; ५२. २६ and ४९; ५४. 8; ५५. ४१; ५९. ९१.
live on air; sages by तपस्; authors of certain सम्हितस्; live in Brahmaloka;
4: Br. II. २५. 4; २६. ४३; ३२. ९९; ३५. ७१ and ९४; III. 1. ५५; १५. १६; IV. 2. २१६.
ऋषिस् by तपस्।
5: M. १२६. ४५; १४५. ९३; २००. 8.
Of the category of सावर्न;
6: वा. ६१. ६२, ८४.
were born out of कुश grass and endowed with all powers in वारुणि यज्ञ;
7: Ib. ६५. ५५; १०१-213.
पुण्या and सुमती are younger sisters of.
8: Ib. २८. ३३.
